s4-3-p6 = prose (cons "This includes program representations, but it does not depend on programming. An integer can be represented by an equivalence class of pairs of natural numbers, a rational by a normalized fraction or an equivalence class of numerator–denominator pairs, a polynomial by a coefficient sequence or a syntax tree, and a finite graph by adjacency data or an incidence relation. Each choice comes with the operations and equalities defining the represented structure. The mathematics of the object is what makes representation independence possible." nil)
